  "tail_bound_derivation": "Couple V=diag(sqrt(a),sqrt(a),sqrt(c))Z, so |V|<=sqrt(a)|Z|. For radial moment p, bound E[|V|^p 1_|V|>R] by (2a)^(p/2) Gamma((p+3)/2,R^2/(2a))/Gamma(3/2). Lorentz preserves radial law. Heat maximum principle puts F(r,xi,t) between its initial angular min and max, hence |log(F/FM)|<=abs(log(a sqrt(c)))+r^2 max(abs(1/2-1/(2a)),abs(1/2-1/(2c))). H tail <=(1+C0)*mass_tail+C2*second_tail+FM_mass_tail. For the fixed-mu parallel marginal, F<=Cinitial exp[-(u^2+2mu)/(2a)] gives Gtail(mu)<=erfc(R/sqrt(2a))/sqrt(a*c)*exp(-mu/a), with m=B=1. Dougherty Gaussian eigenvalues <=a for all t; same coupling bounds apply, with no claim of pointwise spectral positivity.",
